    "API keys are secret Bearer tokens scoped to a project: sk_live_... for production, sk_demo_... for basic evaluation only (a demo key used for an action needing a live key gets 403 demo_api_key). Keep the key on the server; never in browser code or a NEXT_PUBLIC_/VITE_ variable.",
    `Send a code: POST https://api.surge.app/accounts/{account_id}/verifications with {"phone_number": E.164}. TS: surge.verifications.create(accountId, { phone_number }); Python: surge.verifications.create(account_id=..., phone_number=...). The send-and-verify guide omits the account id, but the API reference and the SDK's api.md take it.`,
    'Create returns { id: "vfn_...", phone_number, status: "pending", attempt_count: 0 }. phone_number must match ^\\+[1-9]\\d{6,14}$ (E.164, e.g. +18015551234). The text reads: "Your verification code is 847291. It expires in 10 minutes."',
    'Check a code: POST /verifications/{id}/checks with {"code": six digits, ^[0-9]{6}$}. TS: surge.verifications.check(id, { code }); Python: surge.verifications.check(id=..., code=...). Response { result, verification: { id, phone_number, status, attempt_count } }.',
    "result values: ok (grant access), already_verified (treat as ok), incorrect (show error, allow retry), expired (code older than 10 minutes; offer a new code), exhausted (3 incorrect attempts; create a new verification, never retry the same one). verification.status: pending, verified, exhausted, expired.",
    "The check endpoint answers 200 for ok, 409 for already_verified and 422 for incorrect, expired and exhausted. The SDKs raise typed errors for 4xx (TS APIError with .status and .error; Python APIStatusError with .status_code), so read the result from those responses too.",
    "Create errors: 422 opted_out (number replied STOP; show the error message, which says to text START, and do not retry) and 429 destination_rate_limit (too many codes to this number; wait 10 minutes). TS error.error.error.type/message; Python e.error.type/message.",
    "Codes go out from a shared pool of Surge numbers, so no campaign, toll-free number or sender ID registration is needed and the sender cannot be customized. The sending number can differ between verifications.",
    "Security tips from Surge: log verification.id and result, never the six-digit code; rate-limit resends and checks in the app too, to cap SMS costs.",
    "Sign up at https://hq.surge.app. API keys are under API Keys in the dashboard's left sidebar; the account ID (acct_01j...) is shown at the top of the dashboard."
